Modifications extract the sheath equations and root search into a standalone
library with physical inputs and results. Application-specific array contracts,
boundary response adapters, continuation/restart state, inactive outflow moments,
and population-fraction coupling have been removed. Process termination has
been replaced with status results. Particle flux and current outputs were added.
Subsequent corrections transport upstream electrons along energy-conserving
orbits, share physical profile validation between closures, extend the branch
search to negative surface potentials and nonflat zero-field endpoints, and
label field-energy ranking explicitly as a heuristic.

Other files retain the MIT license in LICENSE unless marked otherwise.

The zero-drift orbit evaluation in src/internal/sheath_model_orbits.f90 and
sheath_model/_orbits.py incorporates the Apache-2.0 BEACH correction 3897f38.
The spectral endpoint and upstream-admissibility work follows BEACH's
feat/spectrum-robust-roots (through 7584aac): cancellation-resistant bin moments,
the two-sided Type-B source coefficient, and a density coordinate restricted
to adjacent floating-point potentials. These ideas are applied to static sheath
physics here; BEACH's Backward Euler update and state management are not included.
test/fixtures/beach_batch154_spectrum.csv and test/test_spectral_endpoint.f90
adapt BEACH's batch-154 regression at 7584aac, including its independent
high-precision static reference values, under Apache-2.0.
